\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces C1 evidence under a common absolute noise level, $480$ paired trials per point or cell. (a)~Matched accuracy (solid) against the free-Jones PEB (dashed) for the three receiver modes. (b)~Paired inlier-conditional efficiency ratio with its $95\%$ paired-bootstrap interval ($4\,000$ replicates, trials resampled in pairs); the shaded band is $\pm 2\%$, the intervals are wider than it, and the scalar curve leaves the plotted range at the two printed values. (c)--(e)~Resolution probability versus delay separation at four Jones overlaps at $-10$~dB, with exact Clopper--Pearson bands; the dashed line is the reference scene's minimum cascaded-delay separation and each panel carries its largest spread across overlap.}}{11}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:c1_combined}{{2}{11}{}{}{}}
