\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces External benchmark with method-consistent continuous refinement, $960$ shared-realization trials per SNR, comparing the proposed MKSC-GI+CCOP-JVP, range-scaled 4-D Jones-VP, ALS-CPD with joint mapping, VBI/SBL with joint refinement, and near-field OMP--SAGE--WLS methods. Each column asks one question of position (top) and of the clock (bottom): precision inside the basin, the shape of the whole error distribution, and the failure rate. (b),~(e)~Empirical complementary CDFs at the $-10$~dB operating point; the dashed line marks the $0.1$-m position threshold and the $1$-ns clock threshold, so where each curve crosses it is that method's rate in~(c) and~(f). (d)~The CEB reference is the median bound of Section~\ref {subsec:res_setup} scaled by $\sigma $. Rate intervals in~(c) and~(f) are the released exact Clopper--Pearson limits; the dotted line is one trial in $960$, hollow markers on it being exact zeros.}}{14}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:benchmark_combined}{{3}{14}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {II}{\ignorespaces Serialized single-thread cost at $-10$~dB: one process, one linear-algebra-library thread, peak resident set size sampled every $10$~ms, $30$ trials per row. Times are means over those trials.}}{14}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:cost}{{II}{14}{}{}{}}
